          definition {
            value: "Identifies the high level taxonomic categorization of the kind of animal."
          }
          comment {
            value: "If the patient is non-human, at least a species SHALL be specified. Species SHALL be a widely recognized taxonomic classification.  It might or might not be Linnaean taxonomy and might or might not be at the level of species. If the level is finer than species--such as a breed code--the code system used SHALL allow inference of the species.  (The common example is that the word \"Hereford\" does not allow inference of the species Bos taurus, because there is a Hereford pig breed, but the SNOMED CT code for \"Hereford Cattle Breed\" does.)."
